summary_used:
Goal: remove songs listed in ~/documents/personal/old_songs.txt from all Spotify playlists and add them to new playlist 'Archived Songs'.

Plan status:
- c1 (read file) and c2 (fetch playlists) are active; c3–c5 pending.
- c1: use file_system.show_file with file_path='~/documents/personal/old_songs.txt' to get the song list.
- c2: use Spotify API to list all playlists.
- c3: for each playlist, determine which tracks are in the old_songs list.
- c4: remove those tracks from each playlist and collect them.
- c5: create new playlist 'Archived Songs' and add all removed tracks to it.

API signatures available (exact):
- file_system.show_file(file_path:string, access_token:string) -> {file_id, path, content, created_at, updated_at}
- file_system.show_directory(access_token:string, directory_path:string?[length >= 1], substring:string?, entry_type:string?[value in ['all','files','directories']], recursive:boolean?)
- spotify.show_playlist_library(access_token:string, is_public:boolean?, page_index:integer?[value >= 0.0], page_limit:integer?[value >= 1.0, <= 20.0]) -> [{playlist_id, title, is_public, rating, like_c...}
- spotify.show_playlist(playlist_id:integer, access_token:string) -> {playlist_id, title, is_public, rating, like_count, review_count, owner, created_at}
- spotify.create_playlist(title:string[length >= 1], access_token:string, is_public:boolean?) -> {message, playlist_id}
- spotify.add_song_to_playlist(playlist_id:integer, song_id:integer, access_token:string) -> {message}
- spotify.remove_song_from_playlist(playlist_id:integer, song_id:integer, access_token:string) -> {message}

Apps explored (do not re-read docs): spotify and file_system API lists already enumerated; no further api_docs calls needed.

Next steps: execute c1 and c2, then proceed to c3–c5 in order.

